## Revision note (attempt 3 — DISPUTE_UPHELD_TEST_WRONG recovery)

The Implementer halted Task 4 with a `TEST_CONTRACT_DISPUTE`: three
`TaskFilter`-shaped literals this suite's attempt-2 `EXISTING_TEST_UPDATED`
fix left in `test/task-filter.test.ts` (lines 45, 83, 134) omitted the new
`q` key, so once `TaskFilter.q` was added as a REQUIRED field
(`q: string | null`, per the PRD Architecture Notes and plan Task 4) they
became `tsc -b` errors (TS2741 at 45/134, TS2345 at 83) — the suite, not the
implementation, was contract-broken. The `code-reviewer` agent arbitrated
the dispute and returned `DISPUTE_UPHELD_TEST_WRONG`, upheld by the owner as
the sanctioned recovery path. Resolution: added `q: null` to all three
literals exactly as the dispute's `proposed_resolution` specified — no
expected value changed, no assertion dropped, no other file touched. See the
extended Lifecycle ledger row below. `npx tsc -b` was re-run in the worktree
after the fix; see the confirmation message for the result.

